            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any aliphatic monocarboxylic acid derived from or contained in esterified form in an animal or vegetable fat, oil or wax. Natural fatty acids commonly have a chain of 4 to 28 carbons (usually unbranched and even-numbered), which may be saturated or unsaturated. By extension, the term is sometimes used to embrace all acyclic aliphatic carboxylic acids.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>CHEBI:13633</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
