            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A disease predisposition that is realized by a disorder development process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">realized disease predisposition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120020 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120020">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120022"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120023"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120054"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A material entity that has one or more pathological disorders as parts; which disorders compose one disease is fixed by the diagnostic classification assigned to them, not by an intrinsic unity criterion. Identity is grounded in the continuity of the disorder lineage, not in momentary material composition (cf. a river persisting through complete material replacement).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">DESIGN RATIONALE - deliberate departure from OGMS. OGMS models disease (OGMS_0000031) as a disposition borne by an organism. MILD does not. Here a disease is a material continuant whose identity is given by the continuity of its disorder lineage, not by a single dispositional potential. Two reasons. (1) Roehl and Jansen show that a disposition-only account breaks on malfunction, because the very disposition said to constitute the disease is the one the bearer has lost. (2) The River Flow Model shows that disease identity persists through complete material replacement, which a single disposition cannot express. MILD keeps what OGMS was built to protect - presymptomatic disease, and the separation of disease from diagnosis and from manifestation - via MILD_120022 pathological disorder under OGMS_0000045 disorder, and via the diagnosis and classification layers. OGMS_0000031 is therefore related but NOT equivalent, and is deliberately not asserted as a parent of this class.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <dc:description xml:lang="en">A material entity that has one or more pathological disorders as parts; which disorders compose one disease is fixed by the diagnostic classification assigned to them, not by an intrinsic unity criterion. Identity is grounded in the continuity of the disorder lineage, not in momentary material composition (cf. a river persisting through complete material replacement).</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A named disease expression may be used for a material disease entity only when it denotes an individual pathological organization in a patient, not merely a diagnostic category, criterion set, behaviour, or social/legal classification. For example, a material substance use disorder case would require a stable pathological neuropsychological organization grounding impaired control and disease course processes; the substance itself and isolated use events are not material disease entities.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">material disease entity</rdfs:label>
        <skos:relatedMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000031"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120021 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120021">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002234"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120022"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120085"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120031"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A process that has as output a pathological disorder and that has as its end boundary a threshold crossing event.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Deliberately no input mandatory. A pre-existing disorder as input would be false for de novo disease (the first disorder has no disorder input).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">disorder development process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120022 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120022">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000045"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120020"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120023"/>
        <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120024"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a disorder is an abnormal presence or organisation of material components — including the limiting case where the abnormal organisation consists in a normally-present component being absent.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:description xml:lang="en">Pathologicity is asserted - not inferred -  by primitives (e.g. threat to life, pain/suffering, loss of ability/fertility) as mentioned by Hucklenbroich et al.</dc:description>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A pathological disorder should not be identified with a merely voluntary, transient, and immediately reversible functional deviation. In substance use disorder cases, the candidate pathological disorder is the relatively stable neurobiological or neuropsychological organization that grounds impaired control, craving, tolerance, withdrawal tendency, or harmful recurrence, not a single act of substance use.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">ExO_0000079 is reused as a comparison anchor rather than as the MILD disease definition: pathological disorder may involve abnormal functioning, abnormal localization of normal functioning, or abnormal localization/organization of constituents relative to relevant members of the same species. Species-comparative abnormality is not sufficient by itself, because rare variation is not automatically pathological.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">pathological disorder</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">a disorder is an abnormal presence or organisation of material components — including the limiting case where the abnormal organisation consists in a normally-present component being absent.</skos:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120023 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120023">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120005"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000197"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120094"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A tendency inhering in a person, grounded in a material basis, whose realization may produce a target pathological disorder.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">Predisposition / risk proper</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <dc:description xml:lang="en">A tendency inhering in a person, grounded in a material basis, whose realization may produce a target pathological disorder.</dc:description>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">disease predisposition</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120024 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120024">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120022"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000312"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120047"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An information content entity that classifies or groups one or more pathological disorders according to diagnostic criteria. Names such as &apos;substance use disorder&apos; can denote this diagnostic layer when used as DSM/ICD-style categories or results; this diagnostic use is distinct from any material disease entity in the patient.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">diagnosis</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <dc:description xml:lang="en">An information content entity that classifies or groups one or more pathological disorders according to diagnostic criteria. Names such as &apos;substance use disorder&apos; can denote this diagnostic layer when used as DSM/ICD-style categories or results; this diagnostic use is distinct from any material disease entity in the patient.</dc:description>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">disease diagnostic result</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120025 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120025">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120047"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000293"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000109"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000293"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120029"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120027"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A disease diagnostic process that has as specified input a measurement datum and a disease threshold specification and that has as specified output a confirmed diseases diagnostic result by objective criteria.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">disease diagnosis process by measurement</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120026 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120026">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120024"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">Trigger finger disease diagnostic result is specified output of some Disease diagnostic process
rdfs:subclass of Confirmed disease diagnostic result by not completely objective criteria</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">a disease conclusion arrived at solely after clinical test can be valid and confirmed but is still inherently subjective because of the subjectivity of clinical tests.</dcterms:description>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">confirmed disease diagnostic result by not completely objective criteria</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120027 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120027">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001909"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120024"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">confirmed diseases diagnostic result by objective criteria</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120028 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MILD/MILD_120028">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
